WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:09.590
When Americans think of national security
they tend to think in terms of military threats.

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:14.750
But national security is also a question of
maintaining a nation's way of life, whether

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:18.390
people have the jobs and the goods that they're
accustomed to.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:23.170
Increasingly we've asked that question in
the context of international trade.

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:26.250
Many of the goods that we buy come from abroad.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:31.060
Each day about 6 million containers of the
kind that you can see behind me arrive in

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:36.019
the United States from other countries carrying
everything from television sets, to clothes,

00:00:36.019 --> 00:00:38.430
to toys, you name it.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:42.670
That globalized economy has turned out to
be both a challenge and an opportunity for

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:43.809
the United States.

00:00:43.809 --> 00:00:47.089
The United States has important comparative
advantages.

00:00:47.089 --> 00:00:49.059
We have a vibrant tech sector.

00:00:49.059 --> 00:00:52.839
And we have the most fertile agricultural
sector in the world.

00:00:52.839 --> 00:00:57.820
Those two sectors through international trade
have generated millions of American jobs.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:01.199
But we also have comparative disadvantages.

00:01:01.199 --> 00:01:05.500
The wage scale in the United States is much
higher than it is in countries like China,

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.720
and India, and Guatemala.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:11.670
That means that those goods often can be produced
more cheaply abroad.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:12.950
That's good for consumers.

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:15.890
We pay less for the goods we buy, as a result.

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:20.860
But it also means that millions of American
jobs have been lost to foreign firms.

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:25.880
The fact that global trade involves winners
and losers has made it one of the most important

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:27.430
policy issues of our time.

